The chemistry is a low-temperature WO₃–ZnO reaction, so plausible phases include unreacted WO₃/ZnO and one or more zinc tungstates; the scan itself will decide this. I’m checking the scientific runtime and extracting peak positions before committing to any structure candidates.

Peak matching is now decisive at the inventory level: the dense monoclinic WO₃ fingerprint matches COD 2311041 line-for-line, while the unmatched peaks form the wurtzite ZnO series; diagnostic ZnWO₄ peaks near 18.9° and 30.4–30.7° are absent. I’m moving to a two-phase Rietveld model and will test whether any systematic residual demands a third phase.

